{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Like birds.</b> The word צפרים is feminine, and if it has a mem [as a suffix pattern], like פילגשים, it is always feminine; therefore עפות." "<b>עפות.</b> An adjective in the participial form, like רצות and שבות (Ezekiel 1:14)." "<b>Will screen.</b> Will protect, from the root of מגן (Genesis 15:1). The meaning concerns the young of the birds, that they will screen over them and deliver them." "<b>And will deliver.</b> A verb [in the participial form] even though it has a chirak." "<b>Hovering.</b> From the root of ופסח יי על הפתח (Exodus 12:23)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:13.755501210Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}